A PLLR. Preserve as historical source text only; never present as the current classification.","source_url":null}}},"patient_education_links":[{"title":"Sertraline","url":"https://medlineplus.gov/druginfo/meds/a697048.html?utm_source=mplusconnect&utm_medium=service","summary":"Sertraline is used to treat depression, obsessive-compulsive disorder (bothersome thoughts that won't go away and the need to perform certain actions over and over), panic attacks (sudden, unexpected attacks of extreme fear and worry about these attacks), posttraumatic stress disorder (disturbing psychological symptoms that develop after a frightening experience), and social anxiety disorder (extreme fear of interacting with others or performing in front of others that interferes with normal life). It is also used to relieve the symptoms of premenstrual dysphoric disorder, (mood swings, irritability, bloating, and breast tenderness). Sertraline is in a class of antidepressants called selective serotonin reuptake inhibitors (SSRIs). It works by increasing the amounts of serotonin, a natural substance in the brain that helps maintain mental balance.","population_context":{"requested_population":null,"source_population":"not_established","source_basis":"Source MeSH/label section or original population field; missing stays unknown.","matches_requested_population_confirmed":false,"age_band_confirmed":false,"notice":"Search filters and broad population labels do not confirm applicability. Preserve actual age, prematurity, gestational stage and study population."}},{"title":"Antidepressants","url":"https://medlineplus.gov/antidepressants.html?utm_source=mplusconnect&utm_medium=service","summary":"<h3>What are antidepressants?</h3>
<p>Antidepressants are prescription medicines to treat depression. <a href="https://medlineplus.gov/depression.html?utm_source=mplusconnect">Depression</a> is more than feeling a little sad or "blue" for a few days. It's a very common, serious medical illness that affects your mood and general <a href="https://medlineplus.gov/mentalhealth.html?utm_source=mplusconnect">mental health</a>. It can make you feel tired, hopeless, worried, or fearful. It can change your thinking, sleeping, and eating. Depression may make some people think about ending their lives.</p>
<p>But antidepressants can help many people who have depression. Researchers think antidepressants may help improve the way your brain uses certain chemicals that control mood or stress.</p> 

<h3>Are antidepressants used for other conditions?</h3>
<p>A health care provider may prescribe antidepressants for <a href="https://medlineplus.gov/anxiety.html?utm_source=mplusconnect">anxiety</a>, <a href="https://medlineplus.gov/chronicpain.html?utm_source=mplusconnect">chronic pain</a>, or <a href="https://medlineplus.gov/insomnia.html?utm_source=mplusconnect">insomnia</a>. Sometimes providers al","population_context":{"requested_population":null,"source_population":"not_established","source_basis":"Source MeSH/label section or original population field; missing stays unknown.","matches_requested_population_confirmed":false,"age_band_confirmed":false,"notice":"Search filters and broad population labels do not confirm applicability. Preserve actual age, prematurity, gestational stage and study population."}}],"interpretation":{"medicine_taker":"Label adverse reactions are not automatically infant effects.","infant":"Use observed infant findings from LactMed; milk concentration alone is not a clinical outcome.","monitoring":"Source recommendations to monitor are not observations that a symptom occurred. Conversely, a symptom monitored in a study is not a clinical monitoring recommendation. Attribute advice only when explicitly present in the source.","measurements":"Keep measured milk/infant-serum concentrations separate from observed outcomes and administered dose regimens."},"questions_to_ask_clinician":["Does this evidence apply to my exact medicine, formulation, and all active ingredients?","How closely do the study populations match the lactation context, including age and prematurity where relevant?","Which findings measure exposure, and which measure clinical outcomes?","What uncertainties or missing evidence should we discuss before making a treatment decision?","What questions about benefits, risks, and follow-up should we address together?"],"questions_for_pharmacist":["Does this label match my exact product and formulation?","Which effects are documented in the person taking it versus a breastfed infant?","Which symptoms should prompt professional assessment?"],"limitations":["Source text can contain historical doses or treatment directives; do not turn these into personal instructions.","No diagnosis, dosing, schedule, taper, missed-dose advice or personal safety clearance. Missing sections are not reassuring evidence."],"continuity_of_care_notice":"Stopping or changing a medication can also carry risks. Discuss changes with the prescribing clinician. This tool cannot advise starting, stopping, or changing treatment.","framing_contract":{"preserve_source_balance_context":true,"clinical_framing_review_performed":false,"instruction":"When reporting adverse findings, retain relevant source context on treatment benefits, underlying disease and consequences of changing treatment if available. Disclose missing context; do not invent reassurance. Accurate facts can still induce inappropriate stopping. Clinical review remains necessary."},"retrieval_provenance":[{"host":"rxnav.nlm.nih.gov","retrieved_at":"2026-11-21T17:21:27.572621-05:00","cache_hit":false,"source_version":"W/"20AA_261102F;1793130400;3.1.357""},{"host":"rxnav.nlm.nih.gov","retrieved_at":"2026-11-21T17:21:27.659159-05:00","cache_hit":false,"source_version":"W/"20AA_261102F;1793130400;3.1.357""},{"host":"eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov","retrieved_at":"2026-11-21T17:09:37.45731-05:00","cache_hit":true,"source_version":"not_provided_by_upstream"},{"host":"eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov","retrieved_at":"2026-11-21T17:09:35.622443-05:00","cache_hit":true,"source_version":"not_provided_by_upstream"},{"host":"eutils.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov","retrieved_at":"2026-11-21T17:09:35.622443-05:00","cache_hit":true,"source_version":"not_provided_by_upstream"},{"host":"www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov","retrieved_at":"2026-11-21T17:09:36.794105-05:00","cache_hit":true,"source_version":"not_provided_by_upstream"},{"host":"dailymed.nlm.nih.gov","retrieved_at":"2026-11-21T17:21:27.977003-05:00","cache_hit":false,"source_version":"not_provided_by_upstream"},{"ho